From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Sun, 20 Feb 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: one-opponent window (Duel.MPWindow, MPBindOpponent,
 MPAssertBound) for Lua at n > 2

At n > 2 a script that reads the other side sees every living opponent. A rule that
needs one opponent (compare with one opponent, one run per opponent) could not say so.

A scope now has a window. While it is open, the reads of the other side (field
class, overlays, counters, hand and Deck, the place prompt) see one duelist:
- kind ONE: the bound opponent of the scope or chain link. Free-for-all only. Tag
  keeps the joined opposing field.
- kind SEAT: an explicit seat (the i-th living opponent after P). Free-for-all and Tag.
An open window with no living seat gives an EMPTY other side (trap W), never every
opponent. A summon procedure scope with a dead bound seat also gives an empty side.

Lua: Duel.MPMode, MPBound, MPOppCount, MPNeedPick, MPBindOpponent(needs_pick),
MPWindow(i), MPWindowEnd, MPAssertBound. MPBindOpponent in a scope that cannot ask
is a Lua error in the trap build (kind c) and false in release. MPAssertBound with
no bound opponent logs trap U.

Lifetime: the window is part of lua_scope. A new scope copies the window only for
the same effect and the same P. scope_guard restores the window of the scope below
on every path (also after a Lua error). A coroutine that waits in a prompt keeps its
window in mp_saved (keyed by lua_State), and the entry is erased when it ends or
fails (the trap build aborts on a leak).

With 2 duelists nothing changes: no scope is pushed and every new branch is
n_duelists > 2.

Review fixes (Opus review of this patch):
- The first run of the activation probe has nothing bound. A ONE window, MPBindOpponent
  and MPAssertBound there now read every opponent / give true and set `touched`, so the
  probe runs the check once per opponent. Before, a target check that opened a window
  never offered the card.
- A new scope of the same effect copies the bound opponent of a ONE window as well.
- Reads of a player value (scope_bound_opp) inside a window with no seat give an
  empty result (a dead-window sentinel): no widening, no pick prompt, no lazy bind.
  lazy_bind and MPBindOpponent use the real binding, not the window seat.
- The core lists of field effects (filter_affected_cards, filter_inrange_cards) ignore
  a window (use mask OPP_EXCL on build_range_list / opp_restrict); the release and
  material lists of the other side (side_cards) follow it.
- MPWindow reads its argument as an integer (257 was seat 1).

