+// needs_pick == false binds nothing (the opposing team is read joined) and gives true. Gives false when no
+// opponent lives. In a context that cannot ask: a Lua error in the trap build (YGO_N_TRAP), false in release; the
+// activation probe is no such context: in its first run (nothing bound) it sets `touched` and gives TRUE (the check
+// errs to yes, the probe runs it again per opponent with that opponent bound).
